          "request": {
            "name": "Amazon Config Put Conformance Pack",
            "description": {
              "content": "<p>Creates or updates a conformance pack. A conformance pack is a collection of Config rules that can be easily deployed in an account and a region and across an organization. For information on how many conformance packs you can have per account, see <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/configlimits.html\"> <b>Service Limits</b> </a> in the <i>Config Developer Guide</i>.</p> <p>This API creates a service-linked role <code>AWSServiceRoleForConfigConforms</code> in your account. The service-linked role is created only when the role does not exist in your account. </p> <note> <p>You must specify only one of the follow parameters: <code>TemplateS3Uri</code>, <code>TemplateBody</code> or <code>TemplateSSMDocumentDetails</code>.</p> </note>",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
